11-///
12-/// A `NOP` names no constant and no block, so its `arg` indexes nothing and is
13-/// free to say this. **Only** this value is a marker: every other operand —
14-/// including the `0` a filler carries — leaves the instruction a filler that
15-/// does nothing. That is what keeps a `NOP` a file happens to contain from
16-/// closing a protected region, running an enclosing `finally` early, or
17-/// truncating the region a failure has to skip.
18-///
19-/// The marker is the maximum `u32`, which is the format's existing "reserved"
20-/// value ([`NO_CONST`](super::NO_CONST), [`NO_BLOCK`](super::NO_BLOCK)): it can
21-/// never be a valid index into a pool or a block list, so it cannot be mistaken
22-/// for one.
